This solution works by first converting the list of candy types into a set, which automatically removes duplicates and gives us the number of unique candy types. Then, it calculates the minimum between the number of unique candy types and half the total number of candies (since Alice can only eat n/2 candies). This ensures that Alice eats the maximum number of different types of candies while following the doctor's advice.

