2. Iterate through the array using three nested loops to generate all possible combinations of indices i, j, and k.
3. Check if the triplet at indices i, j, and k satisfies the three conditions mentioned above.
4. If all conditions are met, increment the count by one.
5. Return the final count of good triplets.

