## Step 1: Problem Description
There are n workers, each with a quality measurement and an expected wage. The goal is to hire exactly k workers to form a paid group. The payment rules are:
1. Each worker in the paid group should be paid in the ratio of their quality compared to others in the group.
2. Every worker in the paid group must be paid at least their minimum wage expectation.

The task is to return the minimum cost needed to form a paid group satisfying these conditions.

## Step 2: Algorithm Overview
- Calculate the captain's ratio (expected wage divided by quality).
- Sort workers by their ratio.
- Iterate from k-1 to n-1 (captain index) to find the k smallest qualities on the left side of the captain.
- Calculate the sum of these k qualities multiplied by the captain's ratio to get the cost for the group.
- Repeat this process for each worker as the captain and keep track of the minimum cost.

## Step 3: Implementation in Code
```cpp
int minCostToHireWorkers(vector<int>& quality, vector<int>& wage, int k) {
    int n = quality.size();
    double minCost = DBL_MAX;

    vector<pair<double, int>> workers;
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        workers.push_back({(double)wage[i] / quality[i], quality[i]});
    }
    sort(workers.begin(), workers.end());

    for (int i = k - 1; i < n; i++) {
        double captainRatio = workers[i].first;
        int sumQualities = 0;
        priority_queue<int> maxHeap;

        for (int j = 0; j <= i; j++) {
            sumQualities += workers[j].second;
            maxHeap.push(workers[j].second);

            if (maxHeap.size() > k) {
                sumQualities -= maxHeap.top();
                maxHeap.pop();
            }

            if (maxHeap.size() == k) {
                minCost = min(minCost, sumQualities * captainRatio);
            }
        }
    }

    return minCost;
}
```

## Step 4: Complexity Analysis
- Time complexity: O(n log n) for sorting + O(n log k) for the main loop, resulting in O(n log n) overall.
- Space complexity: O(n) for storing worker ratios and qualities.

